# Feature branch workflow

When the user is **finishing a feature branch**, **organizing commits**, or **opening a PR**, follow the rules below. Full templates live locally in `requirements/FEATURE_BRANCH.md` (never committed).

## Commits

- Sync the index with the latest edits before committing (`git add` after final edits).
- Use concise Conventional Commits: `type(scope): imperative summary` (≤72 chars, lowercase subject).
- Split by **intent** (feat / fix / refactor / docs / test / chore), not one blob per repo.
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by` or AI attribution trailers unless the user explicitly requests them.
- **Never** commit anything under `requirements/` (`.gitignore` + `.git/info/exclude`).

## Pull requests

- **Title:** one line, same style as a good commit subject.
- **Body:** 2–4 summary bullets + test plan checklist; stay brief.
- Draft PR text in `requirements/PR_DESCRIPTION.md` locally; paste into GitHub manually.

## Local docs (not in git)

- `requirements/FEATURE_BRANCH.md` — commit and PR checklist
- `requirements/FOLLOW_UP.md` — engineering follow-ups
